%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# Dancing with friends and enemies: boids' swarm intelligence
Adapted from [Wolfram Community](https://community.wolfram.com/groups/-/m/t/122095). Written by *Simon Woods*

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
- 1000 dancers assume random positions on the dance-floor.
- Each randomly chooses one "friend" and one "enemy".
- At each step every dancer
  - moves 0.5% closer to the centre of the floor
  - then takes a large step towards their friend and a small step away from their enemy.
- At random intervals one dancer re-chooses their friend and enemy

Randomness is deliberately injected. Here is the dance...

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
- 1000 dancers assume random positions on the dance-floor.
- Each randomly chooses one "friend" and one "enemy".
- At each step every dancer
  - moves 0.5% closer to the centre of the floor
  - then takes a large step towards their friend and a small step away from their enemy.
- At random intervals one dancer re-chooses their friend and enemy

Randomness is deliberately injected. Here is the dance...

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
<span style="color:red">Evaluate initialization cells first</span> or go one by one

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
<span style="color:red">Evaluate initialization cells first</span> or go one by one

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  InitGroup: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
ClearAll[handler, n, r, f, s, x, p , q]

n = 1000;
r := RandomInteger[{1, n}];
f := (#/(.01 + Sqrt[#.#])) & /@ (x[[#]] - x) &;
s := With[{r1 = r}, p[[r1]] = r; q[[r1]] = r];
x = RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {n, 2}];
{p, q} = RandomInteger[{1, n}, {2, n}];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
__Main render function__

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
__Main render function__

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  InitGroup: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
fps = 0;
fpsLabel = "0";
time = AbsoluteTime[];

handler = Function[Null,
  x = 0.995 x + 0.02 f[p] - 0.01 f[q];
  If[r < 100, s];

  (* FPS counter *)
  fps += 1;
  With[{diff = AbsoluteTime[] - time},
    If[diff >= 1.0,
      fpsLabel = ToString[fps / (diff)];
      fps = 0;
      time = AbsoluteTime[];
    ];
  ];
];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
__Drawing function__
Evaluate *this cell very last*

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
__Drawing function__
Evaluate *this cell very last*

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Graphics[{
  PointSize[0.007], Point[x // Offload],
  EventHandler[AnimationFrameListener[x // Offload], handler],
  Text[fpsLabel // Offload, {-1.8,1.8}]
}, PlotRange -> {{-2,2}, {-2,2}}, TransitionType->None]  

